  "body": "The term _relative_ has a different meaning in _a relative URL_ (a string that needs a base URL to be parsed successfully) and _an URL’s non-relative flag_ (which indicates it can not meaningfully be used as a base URL). For example, `http://whatwg.org` is not a relative URL, but it is not non-relative either (its non-relative flag is unset).\n\nTo reduce term overloading, the non-relative flag (and non-relative path state) could be renamed to something else. Maybe _non-hierarchical_? Or just _hierarchical_ and flip the logic. It’s annoying to type and pronounce, but RFC 3986 seems to be using hierarchical for roughly this concept.\n",
